# `yo fix <path> --migrate unsized` (decision 49 S1f; VERDICTS-40 §5,
# VERDICTS-43 §4, VERDICTS-55) writes every bare `Dyn(...)` type spelling as
# `Box(Dyn(...))`, `*Dyn(...)`/`?*Dyn(...)`, an alias body and a
# `size_of`/`Type.eq` argument included, and leaves `Box`/`Rc`/`&`/`&mut`'s
# argument and `upcast`'s target alone. It lists `Rc(Dyn(T)).new(...)`,
# `impl(Dyn(...), ...)` and a spelling over several lines (multi.yo). The
# second run rewrites nothing, and both files still type-check.
fix . --migrate unsized
fix . --migrate unsized
check main.yo
check multi.yo
